ench_engine_step_once_save_const_single_transition/allocations.tsv\nHOST/VARIANCE/ADVERSE OBSERVATIONS:\n# Independent performance review\n\nVerdict: ACCEPT, limited to recorded-session MEAN comparisons for the three declared IR-interpreter metrics. No data, arithmetic, binary/source-identity, or observed busy-guard finding. This is not causal speedup, individual-operation tail-latency, generated/maxperf, release, or whole-product acceptance.\n\nAccepted input is `/home/lewis/tmp/vb-f1f5-final-benchmark-r121/session02` only. Protocol R2 is predeclared ABBA on CPU14, 100 samples per metric per run, 3-second warmup and 5-second measurement. All four latency phases and the candidate-only counter phase record exit 0; all 12 latency logs contain exactly the intended benchmark, 100 samples, and no observed execution error. Both fresh benchmark build receipts and real-operation preflights record exit 0. The Cargo benchmark artifacts are `fresh: false` and use the same bench profile and pinned nightly.\n\n| Metric | Baseline mean ps | Candidate mean ps | Mean delta | Unchanged allowed regression |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| SaveConst step | 43246 | 37890 | -12.385050809% | 3% |\n| IPC frame decode | 70886 | 71233 | +0.490365231% | 5% |\n| Budgeted engine run | 67744 | 58124 | -14.200811039% | 3% |\n\nIndependent exact-rational recalculation uses both original unrounded Criterion `mean.point_estimate` values per side, equal run weighting, then one final conversion/round to integer picoseconds. All 1,200 measured raw samples are retained. P50/P95/P99 are nearest-rank quantiles of the 200 pooled `time/iterations` sample means per side, ranks 100/190/198, not per-operation tails. Calculated values match the aggregate; no outlier/sample removal or run selection occurred. All four cross-pair mean comparisons also remain within each unchanged threshold. IPC's observed mean worsens by 0.490365231%, which must remain visible. Pooled sample-mean p99 is lower in this session for every metric, as are all four per-run cross-pair p99 comparisons; no adverse p99 observation was removed or imported from an older session.\n\nThe candidate is exactly `ae0d8d3afcd2be6a75776a706577902f47f47027`; baseline is `7f505d498fa35acb5b70b083ac6f02cd40f3a891` with only the frozen approved benchmark fixture/harness overlay. Independently scanned actual tracked bytes and modes agree with their pinned Git blobs, except that sole approved baseline benchmark postimage. Recomputed performance fingerprints are baseline `af0335bf81f5c6c07679fc6a1c34aaaeb6bedc36ca8a36b790223aaa2ca41a7f`, candidate `4f671804bda19735129a1bc8ccbaa8c1107da508bbf041c27506d867c08140a3`. Every phase's source-before/source-after and invocation agree with the corresponding build and protocol. Fixture bytes and IPC frame hashes agree across sides. Actual binary/build/preflight hashes and frozen recipe/protocol hashes were checked. Root Cargo.lock and bench settings are shared; no claim is made that the entire root Cargo.toml is unchanged.\n\nAll three actual `instructions:u` logs report 100.00% event running. Instruction counts match the aggregate. Allocation counts equal the complete heaptrack histogram count sums and the printer summaries; allocated byte totals equal the sum of `allocation_size * count` across all histogram rows. All six profiler sample files contain 10 samples; saved invocation commands identify the expected candidate binary and filters, actual logs identify the selected benchmarks, and heaptrack printer receipts identify the debuggee command. These are separate candidate-only, whole filtered Criterion process invocations, including startup, fixture setup, warmup/calibration and measured work. They are neither per-operation counters nor baseline comparisons; perf and heaptrack totals do not describe a single combined invocation. Profiler timings never enter latency means.\n\nHost evidence records AMD Ryzen 9 9950X3D, CPU14 performance governor, SMT sibling30, and ordinary desktop/model processes. Before/after latency snapshots show no competing build/proof in the recorded process rows; each phase also passed the full process-name guard immediately before measurement. Latency vmstat intervals show 88\u201397% whole-host idle, small swap-in, no interval swap-out; resident swapped pages remain. CPU thermal and pressure snapshots, desktop background work, shared caches/SMT, run variance and incomplete continuous per-core attribution prevent claims of an isolated host, absence of every transient interference, absence of throttling, or causal speedup. Counter-phase CPU pressure is higher and is preserved separately. All recorded host data remains available in `host-review.json` and source logs.\n\nSession01 is rejected as a complete protocol attempt: A1/B1/B2 finished, then the A2 premeasurement guard detected cargo-nextest/cargo/rustc and refused before creating A2 measurements. No session01 sample is reused. `session01-failed-A2-guard.log` is a byte-exact copy of the original full failing driver log, `session01-REJECTED.json` preserves its rejection receipt, and `failed-session01-manifest.json` hashes all 108 preserved failed-session files in their original external location. The new session02 repeats the entire ABBA sequence; this is not fast-side selection.\n\nData-only receipts: `recomputed-results.json`, `source-binary-invocation-receipts.json`, `host-review.json`, `input-artifact-manifest.json`, failed-session artifacts, and `REVIEW.sha256`. The accepted session's 218 files were hashed before and after review and remained unchanged. No build targets or binaries were copied. Only this external review directory was written; no repository edits, new measurements, builds, proofs or process control occurred. Performance-policy publication/validation was not executed by this review. Reference: holzman-rust `references/latency-throughput-playbook.md`.\n\n--- UNMODIFIED RAW TEXT {\"decoded_sha256\": \"24239ba179f742cabb936ad1f2107563874f48231e4